{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 41, :comments ["<b>And they shall scrape.</b> רדויי״ר בְּלַעַז, and in Mishnaic language there are many." "<b>From the house.</b> From the inside." "<b>All around.</b> Around the affected spot; so it is expounded in the Targum — that he shall peel off the plaster that is around the stones of the affected spot." "<b>Which they scrape off.</b> A term of edge — which they scraped off at the edges of the affected spot all around."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {0 "The la'az רדויי״ר corresponds to Old French radouir, 'to scrape/smooth.'", 2 "Rashi writes בת״כֹּ, apparently an abbreviation for תרגום כתוב or similar, hence rendered 'in the Targum.' The abbreviation is unusual and its expansion uncertain."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:06:30.655158410Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}